Q2. Given a binary array nums and an integer k, return the maximum number of consecutive 1's in the array if you can flip at most k 0's.

Sol. 
class Solution {
    public int longestOnes(int[] nums, int k) {
        int i = 0 ;
        int zeroes = 0 ;
        int maxlen = 0 ;

        for(int j = 0; j< nums.length ; j++){
            if(nums[j]==0){
                zeroes++;
            }
            while(zeroes>k){
                if(nums[i] == 0){
                    zeroes--;
                }
                    i++;

            }
            maxlen = Math.max(maxlen, j-i+1);
        }
        return maxlen;
    }
}
